To be tax-exempt under the **Income Tax Act, 1961**, an organization must:

- be organized for **religious or charitable purposes**;
- spend **85% of its income** in the financial year on its objects, with 12 months after year end to comply;
- accumulate surplus only for specific projects, for 1 to 5 years;
- not apply income or property for the benefit of the founder, trustee, their relatives or anyone who contributed more than Rs. 50,000 in a financial year;
- file its annual income return on time.
